    "note": "Parameter records: bridge_ef14 builds our EuclideanField from a BlindEuclideanField. The field, the cone and the axioms are the same. The blind Σ-valued sqrt is split into sqrt, sqrt_nonneg and sqrt_square. The bridge forgets the blind extra axiom nonneg_total. In general, there is no map in the other direction, because totality is not one of our axioms. So our version covers a larger class of fields, and no blind statement needs such a map. Over bridge_ef14 K, BlindInnerProductLaws ≃ IsInnerProduct (the fields are reordered). OS and OS_n are equivalent with refl round trips. The function blind_dot is dot_product by refl. The blind 𝕍ⁿ is our standard space up to a path whose space and form components are refl. The proofs of finite dimension and of the laws are different."
