    "note": "The literal blind statement asks for a GroupIso, as data, for every E of dimension n and every point P. It is refuted for n = 2 and every K (bridge_point_symmetry_orthogonal_refuted). A family of isomorphisms Aut(c a) ≅ G over a type makes the images of loops central. Over OS_2 with c = point_object_map, such a family would make O(2) abelian. This contradicts orthogonal_two_not_abelian. The blind statement has no corrected variant. The bridge file defines blind_point_symmetry_orthogonal_corrected, which states the mere existence of the isomorphism. It is derived from our point_symmetry_group. The data version holds at (𝔼ⁿ, {0}) (bridge_point_symmetry_origin, from origin_symmetry_iso). For the corrected and origin versions, the bridge file is bridge-03-geometric-objects."
